<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Live-Wright-II: Lares (Tasked Spirit). A build seat on lane b1-lift. Edit packages/lararium-web/tests/e2e/shore-writes.e2e.test.ts's waitForLivePage (~:208-221) alone. Do not commit.

THE LAW (operator, 2026-11-06: "No timeout, 'No global now'"): no clock decides. A wait ends on the product's own event, never on elapsed time: no `timeout: N`, no silence window, no ceiling, no sleep, no retry loop. Playwright's `{ timeout: 0 }` waits without a clock; the test runner's own job cap stays outside this helper.

THE FAULT (measured, /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/resume.md "Mount-Warden step"): waitForLivePage waits a fixed 20000 ms for a `#phases .phase` reading `live`, then for #mirror data-lar-shown="mirror" with a nonempty `.lar-mirror` pane. A founding boot in CI takes 21.6-27.2 s, progressing phase by phase; every red cut it at 20.2 s. No await hangs.

THE CURE: each wait resolves on its arrival event OR on a terminal event that says it will never arrive, then the helper asserts which:
# Read packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts (the #phases writer, ~:365, and the status/refusal paint), vessel-port.ts and the boot's refusal phases to find every TERMINAL signal the page shows: a refusal or fault phase word, a refusal status line, the `[daemon-island:fault]` console line (browserConsole already collects it), a `pageerror`. Name each with file:line.
# waitForFunction({ timeout: 0 }) on: `live` present OR a terminal signal present. If terminal, fail naming it plus the phases and faults (keep today's message shape). Same for the mirror wait: shown-with-children OR a terminal signal.
# If the page offers no terminal signal for some failure path (a boot that refuses silently), say so in out.md with file:line; do not invent one and do not add product code: that becomes a product row.
Run no browser and no e2e (the controller runs the e2e). Typecheck the file if a tsconfig covers it. Write out.md: the diff summary and the terminal signals found.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

